                        "review": "I really enjoy this game, the physics can be a little weird compared to other games in the genre but overall it feels mostly pretty polished. Most of the campaigns feel a little out of date but they are still pretty fun and give you some rough terrain to overcome. My real problem with the game is just how aggressive the monetization is, and its an issue that gets worse with nearly every single update. The game by itself is very barebones and you need to buy atleast the airborne dlc to be able to get any decent building blocks. Since ive started playing this game, there was only ONE SINGLE TIME that they release an update without putting a paywall up for the new things they added and that was when they added the radio receiver/transmitter blocks. its absolutely horrendous at the moment too the point that if you wanted to get all of the FUNCTIONAL DLC, you would need to spend OVER SEVENTY DOLLARS on a game THAT YOU ALREADY PAID FOR. In it's current state, I cannot recommend this game to anyone whatsoever",
